{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20324",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 7.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.7,
      "end_seconds": 12.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.64,
      "end_seconds": 19.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.75,
      "end_seconds": 24.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.29,
      "end_seconds": 33.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.27,
      "text": "Oh, it's some chest discomfort when I climb stairs. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.27,
      "end_seconds": 36.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.58,
      "end_seconds": 50.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.55,
      "end_seconds": 56.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is it worse at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.1,
      "end_seconds": 61.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Yes, stairs. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.71,
      "end_seconds": 69.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Well, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 69.29,
      "end_seconds": 74.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.19,
      "end_seconds": 84.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "I was getting to that! I've been feeling tired too, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 85.36,
      "end_seconds": 88.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.05,
      "end_seconds": 103.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Any blood in the urine, fainting or pain at rest at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.08,
      "end_seconds": 120.41,
      "duration_seconds": 15.33,
      "text": "No, no blood in the urine, no fainting, no pain at rest. I did have bruising easily at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.21,
      "end_seconds": 126.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any breathlessness or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.31,
      "end_seconds": 130.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.17,
      "end_seconds": 136.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.32,
      "end_seconds": 139.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.35,
      "end_seconds": 146.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.47,
      "end_seconds": 149.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.41,
      "end_seconds": 157.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.68,
      "end_seconds": 161.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "I'm allergic to wheat, I get bloating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.68,
      "end_seconds": 165.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.01,
      "end_seconds": 168.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.88,
      "end_seconds": 169.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.97,
      "end_seconds": 174.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I have heart disease, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.03,
      "end_seconds": 184.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "I follow. Right, so diabetes is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.34,
      "end_seconds": 191.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.18,
      "end_seconds": 196.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.35,
      "end_seconds": 201.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.8,
      "end_seconds": 220.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Alright, what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.85,
      "end_seconds": 231.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.35,
      "text": "Mm, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.82,
      "end_seconds": 235.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.91,
      "end_seconds": 251.76,
      "duration_seconds": 14.85,
      "text": "For my sugar, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 252.67,
      "end_seconds": 263.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "Sorry, um, what was I saying, it's meant to be once a day, though I don't see he take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.93,
      "end_seconds": 268.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "I was on metformin before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.49,
      "end_seconds": 272.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.61,
      "end_seconds": 285.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.88,
      "end_seconds": 312.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.43,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 115 over 73, BMI works out to 37.2, height 153 centimetres. And weight 87 kilos, pulse is 81 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.85,
      "end_seconds": 319.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.87,
      "end_seconds": 321.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.05,
      "end_seconds": 325.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.06,
      "end_seconds": 345.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "There are a few small bruises on your forearms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.06,
      "end_seconds": 349.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.02,
      "end_seconds": 368.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and your chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.26,
      "end_seconds": 402.14,
      "duration_seconds": 29.88,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. So where does that leave us? I don't have a clear answer today: stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding is possible, and so is reflux from the tablets. I want an ECG done, that's for chest discomfort. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for bruising and bleeding. I'll start you on pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. It's for stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.49,
      "end_seconds": 432.45,
      "duration_seconds": 28.96,
      "text": "Take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own. If it hasn't settled next month, we'd think about a lipid profile, but not now. Do get help quickly if you pass black stools or have prolonged bleeding. I'd like to see you again in six weeks. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.22,
      "end_seconds": 436.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}